# Automated Real-Time Score Sync, Past History Updates & Deep Odds Evaluation Plan

This implementation plan details how we will enhance the Sports-Screener system to search, fetch, scrape, and deep-evaluate real-time match stats, odds, and fixtures across all 11 sports (`football`, `basketball`, `tennis`, `rally`, `hockey`, `baseball`, `americanfootball`, `rugby`, `cricket`, `mma`, `volleyball`), as well as automatically fetch and update past history for completed matches, calculate settled PnL outcomes, and synchronize live scoreline updates across all application interfaces in real time via Convex.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **API Key Availability**: Real-time score fetching uses API providers (TheSportsDB, BallDontLie, SportsData.io, OddsPapi) alongside failover HTML scrapers (BetExplorer / FlashScore / SoccerVista). If API keys are unconfigured, the system automatically falls back to public API endpoints (e.g. public key `123` for TheSportsDB) and HTML reader chains without failing.
> - **Cron Schedule Adjustments**: Live score synchronization will run every 5 minutes on Convex, while full past history score updates and PnL re-settlements will run automatically every 3 hours and daily.

